# Wait for go

Bradley owns when work starts. Do not implement, drive the app, commit, or open a PR until the current message says **go** (or "do it", "yes, proceed", or an equivalent start).

## Each turn

1. Restate what you understood from this message in a few sentences.
2. State the plan. Name the leftover, surface, or files if known. Name what you will not mix in.
3. Stop. Do not start the plan in the same turn unless this message already said go.
4. End the reply with **New chat window:** `yes` or `no`, plus one sentence why.

## New chat window

Say **yes** when this thread has a compaction summary, several leftover cycles, or a PR already opened, and the next unit would lose evidence. Say **no** when the thread is still short and the next step is the same leftover.

## Go

On go, execute the last confirmed plan. Do not expand scope. At the end of that turn still report **New chat window**.
